<section class="creator-layout"><header><span class="eyebrow">YOUR WORLD, READY TO PLAY</span><h2>Create &amp; import</h2><p>Build items and World Beings. Stay here to create the next one.</p></header><nav class="swords-nav" aria-label="Import mode"><button type="button" data-action="importTab" data-tab="single">Item Importer</button><button type="button" data-action="importTab" data-tab="mass">Mass Importer</button><button type="button" data-action="importTab" data-tab="world">World Being · Text</button><button type="button" data-action="importTab" data-tab="manual">World Being · Manual</button></nav>{{#if isManual}}<div class="creator-scroll manual-world"><fieldset><legend>Identity</legend><div class="creator-grid"><label>Name<input name="manual.name" value="{{manual.name}}" placeholder="Name your World Being" autocomplete="off"></label><label>Destination folder<select name="manual.folder">{{selectOptions actorFolders selected=manual.folder}}</select></label></div></fieldset><fieldset><legend>{{#if rules21}}Sidhi, Parts &amp; resources{{else}}Resources &amp; movement{{/if}}</legend><div class="creator-grid">{{#each manualStats}}{{#if resource}}<label>{{label}}<input type="number" name="manual.{{key}}" value="{{value}}" min="{{min}}" {{#if max}}max="{{max}}"{{/if}} step="1"></label>{{/if}}{{/each}}</div><p class="creator-hint">{{#if rules21}}Starts unhurt with full Flame. Leave HP per Part and Morale at 0 to use the sheet's own arithmetic; Move, Dash and Speed follow the Cores.{{else}}Starts at full Health, Armor, and Ardor.{{/if}}</p></fieldset><fieldset><legend>{{#if rules21}}Cores{{else}}Cultivations{{/if}}</legend><div class="creator-grid">{{#each manualStats}}{{#unless resource}}<label>{{label}}<input type="number" name="manual.{{key}}" value="{{value}}" min="0" step="1"></label>{{/unless}}{{/each}}</div></fieldset>{{#if rules21}}<fieldset><legend>Cultivations</legend><label>Name and rating, separated by commas<textarea name="manual.cultivations" rows="3" placeholder="Beast Shrine 3, Stillness 2, Red Gun 4">{{manual.cultivations}}</textarea></label><p class="creator-hint">Basic Cultivations go on the sheet by name. Sect Cultivations (Red Gun, Demon Body, …) and any other name are added as Esoteric Cultivations.</p></fieldset>{{/if}}<fieldset data-manual-loadout class="manual-loadout"><legend>Starting items</legend><p>Drag items here from the compendium browser or Items directory.</p><button type="button" data-action="browseManualItems">Open compendium browser</button><ul class="creator-queue">{{#each manualItems}}<li><span>{{name}} <small>{{type}}</small></span><button type="button" data-action="removeManualItem" data-index="{{index}}">Remove</button></li>{{else}}<li class="creator-hint">{{#if rules21}}Drop weapons, armor, Assets, Traits, Technicks, Magicks, or other items here.{{else}}Drop weapons, Fashion, Traits, Technicks, Magicks, or other items here.{{/if}}</li>{{/each}}</ul><p class="creator-hint">Items start inactive so entered stats are not counted twice. Equip or activate them on the finished sheet.</p></fieldset></div><footer class="creator-footer"><p role="status">{{manualStatus}}</p><button type="button" class="creator-primary" data-action="createManualWorldBeing">Create World Being</button></footer>{{else}}{{#if isSingle}}<div class="creator-scroll"><fieldset><legend>Item identity</legend><div class="creator-grid"><label>Destination folder<select name="folder">{{selectOptions folders selected=folder}}</select></label><label>Item type<select name="itemType">{{selectOptions types selected=type}}</select></label><label>Name<input name="name" value="{{name}}" required placeholder="Name your item" autocomplete="off"></label></div></fieldset><fieldset><legend>Details</legend><div class="creator-grid">{{{fields}}}</div></fieldset><fieldset><legend>Description &amp; abilities</legend><prose-mirror name="system.description" value="{{description}}"></prose-mirror></fieldset><p class="creator-hint">Use Edit last created for artwork, Active Effects, and drag-and-drop weapon mods.</p></div><footer class="creator-footer">{{#if batch}}<details open><summary>Batch queue ({{batch.length}})</summary><ul class="creator-queue">{{#each batch}}<li>{{name}} · {{type}} <button type="button" data-action="removeQueued" data-index="{{index}}">Remove</button></li>{{/each}}</ul><button type="button" data-action="createBatch">Import queued items</button></details>{{/if}}<p role="status" aria-live="polite">{{#if lastName}}Created {{lastName}} · {{count}} this session{{else}}Items are saved to the Items directory.{{/if}}</p><div>{{#if lastName}}<button type="button" data-action="editLast">Edit last created</button>{{/if}}<button type="button" data-action="queue">Add to batch</button><button type="submit" class="creator-primary">Create item</button></div></footer>{{else}}<div class="creator-scroll"><fieldset><legend>{{#if isWorld}}World Being stat blocks{{else}}Mass Importer{{/if}}</legend>{{#if isWorld}}<p class="creator-lead">Paste a stat block, preview the result, then import.</p><div class="import-steps"><span><b>1</b> Add text</span><span><b>2</b> Review</span><span><b>3</b> Create</span></div><details class="import-help"><summary>Formatting &amp; item matching</summary>{{#if rules21}}<p>Rules 2.1 Bestiary layout. Each block starts with <b>NAME ✦ genus</b> and <b>SIDHI X</b> (or X/Y/Z), then the Move, Speed and Parts lines, then the headed sections: ARMOR, WEAPONS, CORES, CULTIVATIONS, LICENSES, ASSETS, TRAITS, DROPS. Paste several blocks at once.</p><p>A block printed as SIDHI 0/3/5 holds three World Beings. Choose below whether to make all of them or one.</p><p>Printed Part HP, Soak, Move, Morale and Flame are stored as printed. Weapons arrive readied. Licenses and Assets are matched by name against your world and visible compendiums; anything not found is made from the stat-block text.</p><p>When reading the rulebook PDF, keep <b>Read columns separately</b> ticked: the Bestiary is set in two columns.</p>{{else}}<p>Start each block with an uppercase name, followed by HEALTH, Cultivations, and bracketed item sections. You can paste several complete blocks at once.</p><p>Items match your world first, then visible compendiums. Microcosmic Orbit uses Technicks and Magicks. Missing items become placeholders.</p><p>Read a PDF below, paste copied text, or upload a text file. Review OCR results before importing.</p>{{/if}}</details>{{#if rules21}}<div class="creator-grid"><label>Sidhi versions<select name="import.versions">{{selectOptions versionChoices selected=importState.versions}}</select></label></div>{{/if}}{{else}}<p class="creator-lead">Add your items, preview the results, then import.</p><div class="import-steps"><span><b>1</b> Add text</span><span><b>2</b> Review</span><span><b>3</b> Create</span></div><details class="import-help"><summary>Formatting &amp; multiple items</summary>{{#if rules21}}<p>Rulebook text is read in the Rules 2.1 layouts:</p><ul><li><b>Sect entries</b> — a title ending in Technick, Magick or Gear, then LICENSE and NEEDS lines (Magicks: MANTRA, MUDRA, CHECK, CHARGE TIME, EFFECT).</li><li><b>Item cards</b> — a line such as <i>2 KG UNCOMMON BASE CLEAVER 500♄</i>, the name, an optional Mods line, then the text. Armor reads its <i>soak_ ⛨⛨</i> line.</li><li><b>Assets</b> — the d66 code, the Star range, the name, then the text.</li><li><b>Labelled</b> — one <i>Name:</i> line per item, with any of Type, Rarity, Weight, Price, Profile, Mods, Soak, Covers, License, Needs, Mantra, Mudra, Check, Charge Time.</li></ul><p>Several entries can be pasted at once; a line of --- also separates them. The default item type only decides entries with no recognisable layout. When reading the rulebook PDF, keep <b>Read columns separately</b> ticked.</p>{{/if}}<ol><li>Choose a format and default item type. For book Traits, choose Rulebook text and Trait.</li><li>Paste complete entries including their numbered headings (for example, 2 4 Adamance). For unnumbered entries, use a Name: heading for each item or a line containing --- between entries.</li><li>Preview and check the count and names. If multiple items appear as one, add separators and preview again.</li><li>Review the editable JSON, then import. The window stays open.</li></ol></details><div class="creator-grid"><label>Destination folder<select name="folder">{{selectOptions folders selected=folder}}</select></label><label>Format<select name="import.format">{{selectOptions formats selected=importState.format}}</select></label><label>Default item type<select name="import.type">{{selectOptions types selected=importState.type}}</select></label></div>{{/if}}<details class="import-help"><summary>Read a PDF / scanned pages</summary><div class="creator-grid"><label>PDF file<input type="file" name="pdf.file" accept=".pdf,application/pdf"></label><label>PDF page numbers<input name="pdf.pages" placeholder="e.g. 214-216, 220"></label></div><p class="creator-hint">Use PDF page numbers, which may differ from printed page labels. Up to 20 pages per read; files up to 250 MB (a large book can take a while to open). English OCR runs locally in your browser.</p><label class="creator-check pdf-ocr-toggle"><input type="checkbox" name="pdf.columns" {{#if pdfColumns}}checked{{/if}}><span>Read columns separately</span></label><p class="creator-hint pdf-ocr-hint">For two-column pages: reads the left column top to bottom, then the right. Untick for single-column pages that come out scrambled.</p><label class="creator-check pdf-ocr-toggle"><input type="checkbox" name="pdf.ocr"><span>Force OCR</span></label><p class="creator-hint pdf-ocr-hint">Use when extracted text is broken or garbled.</p><div class="pdf-actions"><button type="button" data-action="readPdf">Read PDF into text</button><button type="button" data-action="cancelPdf">Cancel reading</button></div><p data-pdf-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p class="creator-hint">Reading appends text below. Correct names, columns, symbols, and numbers before previewing.</p></details><label class="import-upload">Upload files <span class="creator-hint">Optional · TXT, JSON, CSV</span><input type="file" name="import.files" multiple accept=".json,.csv,.txt"></label><label>Paste source text<textarea name="import.content" rows="10" placeholder="Paste your complete entries here…">{{importState.content}}</textarea></label><button type="button" data-action="previewImport">Preview entries</button></fieldset><p role="status">{{importState.status}}</p>{{#if importState.names}}<fieldset><legend>Detected entries ({{importState.names.length}})</legend><ol>{{#each importState.names}}<li>{{this}}</li>{{/each}}</ol></fieldset>{{/if}}{{#if importState.notes}}<details><summary>Review notes</summary><ul>{{#each importState.notes}}<li>{{this}}</li>{{/each}}</ul></details>{{/if}}<details class="import-help"><summary>Advanced: edit preview JSON</summary><label>Preview data<textarea name="import.review" rows="16">{{importState.review}}</textarea></label></details><p>Nothing is created until you press Import preview. Successful entries leave the preview; failed entries remain available to correct.</p></div><footer class="creator-footer"><button type="button" class="creator-primary" data-action="commitImport">Import preview</button></footer>{{/if}}{{/if}}</section>